== Fashion E-commerce

As established in the Introduction, the scale of global fashion e-commerce (770 billion USD in 2024, approaching one trillion by 2030) and the 30 percent search abandonment rate expose a critical interface failure: the text search bar. Fashion is inherently visual. Consumers make purchase decisions based on aesthetic attributes (silhouette, drape, colour relationship, print density) that keyword matching cannot adjudicate. Platforms such as ASOS, Zalando, and Shopee have invested in visual search precisely because their catalogues contain millions of SKUs indexed by inconsistent, vendor-supplied metadata. The business case for visual search in fashion is therefore not academic: it addresses a direct revenue leakage from search abandonment. This section positions the problem domain within the broader industry context.
